<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Odoacer</h1><p class="st-meta">476 CE – 493 CE · capital Ravenna</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Kingdom of the barbarian general Odoacer, who deposed the last western emperor, Romulus Augustulus, in 476 and ruled Italy until 493.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a>, an officer of Germanic origin in the Roman army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, led a mutiny of soldiers demanding land. In 476 he defeated the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orestes-roman-general">Orestes</a> and deposed his son, the young emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a>, sending the imperial regalia to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeno-emperor">Zeno</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. His soldiers proclaimed him king.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> ruled from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-ravenna">Ravenna</a> as king while nominally recognising the eastern emperor. He kept the Roman administration and the Senate, appointing Roman consuls and officials, and gave his soldiers land, traditionally a third of estates. An Arian Christian, he tolerated the Catholic Church. He gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a> by treaty, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> and destroyed the Rugian kingdom on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> in 487.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeno-emperor">Zeno</a> sent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-the-great">Theodoric</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrogoths">Ostrogoths</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> in 489. After defeats on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soca">Isonzo</a> and at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-verona">Verona</a>, Odoacer held out in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-ravenna">Ravenna</a> for three years. He agreed to share power in 493 but was killed by Theodoric at a banquet days later, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ostrogothic-kingdom">Ostrogothic Kingdom</a> replaced his.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-odoacer.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Odoacer" width="320" height="284"><figcaption>Image: Shuaaa2 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Italy_-_476_to_479_AD.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>476 CE – 493 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ravenna</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Odoacer</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Arian and Nicene Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>, <a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a>, <a href="/countries/croatia">Croatia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Italy (Odoacer), Odoacer's Italy</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=484&amp;focus=kingdom-of-odoacer" aria-label="Kingdom of Odoacer on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4972 607 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Odoacer lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5292 863L5304 942M5292 863L5709 970M5292 863L5292 863"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0M5709 970h0M5292 863h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5292 863h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5292 863h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ravenna. <a href="/atlas?year=484&amp;focus=kingdom-of-odoacer">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
